        "prerelease": false,
        "public_excerpt": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s-8d26bb1df91b23ce",
      "kind": "release",
      "title": "v3.4.1",
      "url": "https://github.com/umami-software/umami/releases/tag/v3.4.1",
      "collected_at": "2026-11-21T07:21:22+00:00",
      "published_at": "2026-10-23T08:26:44Z",
      "text": "Umami `v3.4.1` is mainly a **security hotfix**. It updates vulnerable dependencies and the Docker base image. All self-hosted users should upgrade.\n\n## Security\n\n- Upgraded Next.js to `16.4.2` (from `16.3.4` in v3.4.0). This fixes a critical RCE in `next/og`, SSRF in image optimi",
      "links": [],
      "metadata": {
        "tag": "v3.4.1",
        "prerelease": false,
        "public_excerpt": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s-9159d45f7a68fb8c",
      "kind": "release",
      "title": "v3.4.0",
      "url": "https://github.com/umami-software/umami/releases/tag/v3.4.0",
      "collected_at": "2026-11-21T07:21:22+00:00",
      "published_at": "2026-09-17T04:21:49Z",
      "text": "Umami `v3.4.0` is here with new **Annotations**, **MCP support**, API key management, a typed API client, session property segments, and security, analytics, and UI improvements.\n\n## New features\n\n### Annotations\n\nAdd dated notes to your website charts to keep launches, campaigns",
      "links": [],
      "metadata": {
        "tag": "v3.4.0",
        "prerelease": false,
        "public_excerpt": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s-3d4ead6cabb92581",
      "kind": "release",
      "title": "v3.3.1",
      "url": "https://github.com/umami-software/umami/releases/tag/v3.3.1",
      "collected_at": "2026-11-21T07:21:22+00:00",
      "published_at": "2026-08-20T18:26:22Z",
      "text": "Umami `v3.3.1` is a maintenance release focused on safer upgrades, tracking correctness, analytics accuracy, and UI fixes.\r\n\r\n## Updates\r\n\r\n- Hardened two-factor authentication when **TWO_FACTOR_ENCRYPTION_KEY** is missing or invalid, with safer API enforcement and clearer config",
      "links": [],
